jobDescription:
DXN Holdings Bhd is the investment holdings and management company of DXN Group. Based in Malaysia, with worldwide operations of 79 subsidiaries across 48 countries.
DXN is principally involved in the sales of health-oriented and wellness consumer products through a direct selling model. It operates a vertically integrated production facilities, right from research and development to cultivation, manufacturing, and distribution. DXN's other business activities that primarily serve to support their core business include conducting laboratory testing services for third parties, offering of lifestyle products, and operating a cafe.
Under its massive expansion programme, we are currently looking for a diligent and experienced
Chief Operating Officer
with the opportunity to develop a professional future career growth within the group to be based in,
preferably
Alor Setar
,
but Petaling Jaya or Cyberjaya can be considered.
The objectives of this role:
Collaborate with CEO in driving the organizational vision and succession plan into achieving the objectives of the Group;
Develop overall operational plan with strategies for implementation and to monitor the performance accordingly;
Ensure effective recruiting, onboarding, professional development, performance management, and retention;
Ensure intellectual properties are properly registered and secured;
Ensure compliance with national and local rules and regulations.
Responsibilities:
Oversee operation, HR and legal functions of the Group;
Implement operational plan with strategies that are in alignment with the short and long-term objectives;
Ensure product registrations for launching of new/existing products;
Ensure regular update on the registration of intellectual properties;
Analyze internal operation and identify areas for process enhancement;
Monitor performance with corrective measures for improvement;
Build and maintain trusting relationships with key customers, clients, partners, and stakeholders.
Required skills and qualifications:
Five or more years of experience in executive leadership roles such as COO, VP of Operations, etc.
Excellent leadership skills, with steadfast resolve and personal integrity.
Understanding of advanced business planning, regulatory issues, and experience within the manufacturing/direct selling sectors.
Solid grasp of data analysis and performance metrics.
Ability to diagnose problems quickly and foresee potential issues.
Excellent analytical and planning skills.
Preferred skills and qualifications
International business experience.

Accurately and promptly collect information on competitors, customers, and the industrial chain market, organize and report it; establish a rich source of data information channels;
Combine the information from research and communication to analyze the market layout and the situation in key areas, judge the changes in market trends, write market analysis reports, and provide support for sales work and future market planning;
According to the leadership's requirements, combine market development and business needs to periodically carry out special market insights, customer needs, and other specific research plans, implement the research, produce research reports, and propose corresponding strategic suggestions;
Organize and collect monthly market reports and monthly sales analysis reports on time;
Timely complete other tasks arranged by the leadership.
Job Requirements:
Minimum 2-3 years working experience in sales or production analysis for Manufacturing company.
Proficient with SQL software.
Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively within an executive team.
Meticulous attention to detail and excellent organizational skills.
Exceptionally proficient in both written and spoken English and Mandarin.
Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, Word, Power point, etc.

Description
Bioinformatics scientists analyse biological processes using computer programmes. They maintain or construct databases containing biological information. Bioinformatics scientists gather and analyse biological data and may also assist scientists in various fields, including in biotechnology and pharmaceutics. They perform scientific research and statistical analyses, and report on their findings. Bioinformatics scientists may also collect DNA samples, discover data patterns and conduct genetic research.
Company
Quantum Bioinformatics sdn bhd. develops and commercializes scientific business intelligence software for biotechnology companies globally, for the integration, mining, analysis, modeling and simulation, management and interactive reporting of scientific data. We are a company that combines financial stability and a strong market position in bioinformatics solutions. Apart from the abovementioned, our company aims to provide leading edge bioinformatics products for various applications including microarray, proteomics, Glycomics and other related areas. In addition, we plan to provide the computational tools for Clinical Medicine in the areas of diagnostics and prognostics. Chishti Malangee also provides computational solutions for better decision making and knowledge management in the life science industry.
Our flexible and comprehensive solutions provide access to relevant knowledge at the right time and in the right context.
Main missions include:
• Managing a computing infrastructure dedicated to scientific computing ;
• Providing advice and support in data analysis (genomic, transcriptomic, metagenomic, annotation, etc.);
• Designing and developing information systems for processing and analysing data ;
• Training investigators in the application of bioinformatics tools.

Working with Liege Solutions and its partners in Australia you will be part of a large team of data specialists and information technology experts who use the power of data to help organisations deliver a smarter, stronger future. Their reputation, built over 25 years, is for excellence in providing data services, higher education research management and hosting and data assurance services. Together with our client, we are delivering business critical systems and transforming the way people live, work, grow and learn through our core areas of expertise:
The Role
This is a full-time hybrid role of Senior Systems Administrator. The Senior Systems Administrator will be responsible for the day-to-day technical administration, ensuring the reliability, stability and security of all systems.
Our partner in Australia is offering a rewarding career opportunity for excellent experiences as a
Senior Systems Administrator
supporting Client’s IT Infrastructure during an exciting transformation period. The position entails working with the ICT Manager to ensure that the Network and Information Technology Infrastructure works in an efficient and secure manner in accordance with the Policies set out by DCA Management.
Key responsibilities include:
Network services planning, deployment and support;
Work with Development teams to migrate workloads to Azure;
Hardware Upgrades and System maintenance;
M365 and Azure administration;
ICT Monitoring;
Prepare Capital Expenditure Requests for Infrastructure Upgrades and Expansion and manage purchase and deployment;
Ensure Operating System and Application upgrades are deployed throughout the organisation;
Firewalls and Remote Access;
Deploy new hosted systems for clients and corporate services;
Provide support and leadership for other ICT staff;
Supporting Automation and Development Operations initiatives; and
Contributing to a continuous improvement culture.
Highly desirable experience includes:
Microsoft Active Directory Administration
All Facets of Microsoft Server administration
Strong understanding of network fundamentals such as TCP/IP, DHCP, DNS etc
Experience with M365 and Cloud Services including Azure and AWS;
Experience in MS Exchange;
Firewall administration;
Proxy design deployment and support;
Server and end-point automation (eg SALT); and
Windows and Linux advanced administration skills.
Cisco Network and Security certifications;
We are seeking an experienced and passionate Information Technology professional ready to advance their technical and leadership skills in a positive and supportive culture. If you are successful in this role, you will enjoy:
A supportive and friendly team environment;
Flexible work arrangements
Travel opportunities
Stability to develop your career in a growth focused company
A range of benefits as part of our Employee Benefit Program.
A competitive remuneration package is on offer and will be based on the successful candidate's experience, skills and knowledge.

